Conclusion: the next 90 days are decisive
The structural picture is clear: voluntary self-governance at frontier AI labs has failed under commercial
pressure, 
 federal safety infrastructure is being deliberately weakened, and the gap is
being filled by a patchwork of state laws, 
 EU regulations, and Palantir-style government integration that
prioritizes capability over safeguards. The safety researchers who understood these systems best are walking out
the door. 
For CSOAI/EI³, the actionable timeline is compressed. The NIST CAISI request for information on AI agent
security closes March 9— 
submitting substantive comments would establish institutional
credibility. The EU AI Act's high-risk enforcement deadline of August 2, 2026 
 creates a six-month
window to build compliance certification services. New York's RAISE Act incident-reporting requirements
